{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_gems_manual_po_frontend_notes", "label": "GEMS Manual PO frontend notes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_no_frontend_flag", "label": "No frontend feature flag for GEMS Manual PO", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A frontend flag was considered and removed: client-side route gating duplicated a control the backend already owns and created one unsafe combination (frontend off, backend on) where CS received emails with links they could not open. The single control is the backend GEMS_MANUAL_PO_FLOW env var.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_capability_booleans", "label": "canApprove / canManualSourcing capability booleans", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Behaviour must never be derived from serverGroups === 'GEMS': with the flag off, Management legitimately approves GEMS QCFs (config qcf_approval_level = 'category leader, management'), so identity-based gating becomes wrong the moment the flag flips. serverGroups and clApprovedAt are display-only.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_qcf_approved_semantics", "label": "qcfApproved vs clApprovedAt semantics", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "qcfApproved does not mean \"CL approved\": it is 1 only after SAP sync succeeds and 2 for Manual Sourcing, and CL approval is rolled back if sync fails, so clApprovedAt is the authoritative post-CL signal.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_is_cs_token_read_only", "label": "isCsTokenReadOnly in QuotationSummaryCL.vue", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Role alone (CS + route token) selects the read-only view deliberately: a CS has no approval capability on any QCF, and keying off the token's purpose claim would send a CS holding a forwarded CL/Management link down a path that returns 400 for them.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_cs_qcf_detail_token_endpoint", "label": "GET /pr/cs/qcf_detail/token/:token (CS read-only QCF detail)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_token_error_code_handling", "label": "Token route error_code handling (TOKEN_EXPIRED, NOT_AUTHORIZED, QCF_NOT_FOUND)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A bare 401 with no error_code is treated as a lapsed CS session (redirect to /login preserving the deep link) because an expired session and an expired token are both 401 and absence of the field is the only signal; it is scoped to CS because the CL/Management token endpoints predate the error_code convention. Flagged as brittle - the backend should attach an explicit error_code on session expiry.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_waiting_manual_po_status_rendering", "label": "Waiting Manual PO status colour mapping and dashboard filter (keep after rollback)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_additive_response_fields", "label": "Additive response fields (serverGroups, clApprovedAt, statusMilestone, canManualSourcing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_return_url_persistence", "label": "returnUrl persistence and getSafeReturnUrl (SSOCallbackHandler open-redirect fix)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Pre-existing bugs affecting every role: the OAuth round trip dropped the stored deep link, and SSOCallbackHandler redirected without open-redirect validation; both fixes are permanent and survive the Manual PO rollback.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_management_dashboard_default_filter", "label": "Management dashboard default status filter unset", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The status filter holds a single value, so the previous 'Need Action' default hid GEMS rows sitting in Waiting Manual PO; the default is now unset (all statuses) while the existing table sort still floats Need Action to the top.", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_dual_flag_qa_matrix", "label": "Dual flag-state QA matrix (Flag ON / Flag OFF)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-frontend/docs/gems-manual-po.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_frontend_docs_gems_manual_po_gems_manu